        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1845-08-11",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "11 August 1845",
        "text": "And Albert wearies too--it seems all false, all writing--not the first part, though.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s3253",
        "messageOrdinal": 189,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-01-06",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "6 January 1846",
        "text": "'People say,' I used to think, 'that women always know, and certainly I do not know, and therefore ... therefore.'--The logic crushed on like Juggernaut's car.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s3772",
        "messageOrdinal": 207,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-01-22",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "22 January 1846",
        "text": "I could not help smiling when I heard of it.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s5753",
        "messageOrdinal": 297,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-04-04",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "4 April 1846",
        "text": "Oh, my two letters—and to turn from such letters to you, to my own Ba!—I very well know I am not grateful enough, if there is any grace in that, any power to avert punishment, as one hopes!",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s6573",
        "messageOrdinal": 329,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-04-27",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "27 April 1846",
        "text": "Pure nonsense I write to you, it seems to me.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s6926",
        "messageOrdinal": 345,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-05-07",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "7 May 1846",
        "text": "A most glorious confusion I was in ... when suddenly my visitor thought of spelling the name ...",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s7622",
        "messageOrdinal": 379,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-05-29",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "29 May 1846",
        "text": "Why do you not see what God sees?",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s7699",
        "messageOrdinal": 383,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-05-30",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "30 May 1846",
        "text": "I am fond of them, but would rather, rather, not see them just now, and not be seen by them—for eyes have they, and can see.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s8387",
        "messageOrdinal": 412,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-06-18",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "18 June 1846",
        "text": "Do pain me so again and again,—if you will so cure me every time!",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s10603",
        "messageOrdinal": 498,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-08-13",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "13 August 1846",
        "text": "A fulness of sympathy, a sharing of life, one with another, ... is scarcely ever looked for except in a narrow conventional sense.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s11828",
        "messageOrdinal": 541,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-09-05",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "5 September 1846",
        "text": "It seems to me that you and I are at one upon the whole question,—only that I am your Flush, and he is mine.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s12500",
        "messageOrdinal": 572,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-09-19",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "19 September 1846",
        "text": "I tried to leave them, and I could not.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      }
    ]
  }
}
